did you know that the European Union has  a total budget of around 140 billion  euros each year it's a lot of money but  on the other hand it represents only  around 1% of the union's wealth and this  budget goes to improving our everyday  life but now  it serves to stimulate the economy and  create jobs to modernize agriculture to  preserve and manage our natural  resources to fight against terrorism  organized crime and illegal immigration  to promote and protect our cultural  heritage but also to help the  development of countries outside the  Union or on a one-off basis in case of a  natural disaster and contrary to popular  belief the union's expenditure  represents only six percent of the total  budget  at every stage the budget is decided  democratically the European Commission  draws up the draft budget and submits it  to the ministers of the EU states within  the council and to the elected  representatives within the European  Parliament not everything is decided in  Brussels most of the projects financed  are chosen and managed by the Member  States where problems arise the European  Commission intervenes and can impose  Corrections  despite its complexity the process is  completely transparent  the accounts of the European Union are  published every year and the whole  budget is controlled by the European  Court of Auditors the Commission alone  is responsible for its management before  the European Parliament which has the  power to sanction it in case of  shortcomings moreover each citizen has  the possibility of checking the  beneficiaries of the EU budget in each  country on the web since it's your right  to ask questions and our duty to answer  them
 

